WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.934
New this morning,

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.701
the Wagner

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.569
military group

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.770
is threatening to leave

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.839
the Ukrainian city of Bakhmut

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.639
This is in the eastern

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.307
part of the country

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:07.741
where we've seen

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.242
some of the fiercest fighting.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.143
Wagner's leader

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.344
Yevgeny Prigozhin

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.479
says his troops

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.280
are running out of ammunition.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.615
So this private military group

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.683
has played a key role

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.418
in Russia's war in Ukraine,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.619
but they've also been engaged

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.587
in this backroom

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.922
bickering with the Russian Defense

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.158
Ministry. With me now is retired U.S.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.626
Army Brigadier General Steve Anderson.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.161
General,
thanks so much for being with us.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.763
Two questions about this claim

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.231
from the volunteer group here.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.698
Number one,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.832
and I'm not sure we believe them,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.566
first of all,

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.635
but if you did pull out of Bakhmut,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.569
what would that mean

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.171
for the military situation there?

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.040
But two, and perhaps more importantly,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.074
what does this bickering

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.275
tell us about discipline

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.643
and coordination inside

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.511
the Russian military?

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.380
Well, thank you, John.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.248
What it tells us

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.450
is that it's a really bad army

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.751
and they've got a lot of issues.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.086
I mean, mercenaries

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.721
make great security guards.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.122
They don't make good soldiers.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.624
And we're seeing that play out

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.425
right here.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.093
I mean, obviously,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:00.527
this is

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.128
be a terrible blow

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.596
to the Russian military.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.397
They're trying to fight

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.199
for the city of buck moot.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.267
I can imagine

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.334
if General Patton

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.402
in the middle of his assault

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.538
on Germany in 1944 and said, you know,

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.440
I'm not getting all the ammo I need,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.607
I'm pulling a third army

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.542
out of this fight here.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.509
I mean, it's ridiculous.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.177
It just shows

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.579
how poorly led, how poorly equipped,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.949
how poorly trained and what a bad army

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.117
the Russian army is.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.285
They're ten years away

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.620
from being a competent fighting force.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.022
General, a key

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.757
piece of reporting from our Alex Moore.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.925
Mark Warner, senior Pentagon

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.393
reporter, and his team

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.929
saying that the Ukrainians on the ground

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.396
and U.S.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.764
officials are concerned

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.033
that the Russians have been able to jam

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.468
electronically jammed

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.603
the guidance system of the high Mars.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.071
This is the artillery rocket system

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:45.572
that the U.S.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.339
has been providing

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.107
to the Ukrainians

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.608
that that has shown some success

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.409
on the ground.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.044
How significant would that be?

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.613
Well, it is significant.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.914
I mean, you need the high marks

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.382
to conduct the deep strikes

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.317
that they're going to need.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.418
I mean,
if they're going to conduct

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.120
a counteroffensive,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.154
they're going to have to achieve

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.755
a breakthrough somewhere

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.891
and they're going to have to use their

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.061
superior maneuver and their ability

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.829
to integrate indirect fire,

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.297
direct fire and aviation.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.532
And of course, the high Mars

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.434
is a very key component

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.669
of this indirect fire capability.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.705
My big concern about the high margin

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.306
is the maintenance requirements.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.407
I mean, my understanding

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.775
is that many of them,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.176
perhaps

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:26.112
as much as 50%, are not operational.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.447
We don't have the

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.848
maintenance capability

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.682
and the repair parts

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.551
to keep those things operational.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.352
The jamming, though,

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.586
of course, is an issue.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.655
We just need more high margin systems

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.356
and we need to

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.290
use those time,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.491
our systems effectively,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.692
and that means maintaining them

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.994
appropriately.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.495
You talked about this

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.230
potential Ukrainian counteroffensive

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.498
here. I have a map of Ukraine.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.733
I just want to show people that, yep,

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.067
a river here, which is this key,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.903
one of the world's key waterways,

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.971
but a strategically important waterway

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.139
in Ukraine right now,

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.841
you can see it divides

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.176
the Ukrainian forces

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.377
and the Russian forces

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.145
toward the south of the country.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.980
Where do you think it would be important

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.882
for Ukraine to strike if it can?

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:04.951
Well,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.053
they're got about a 400 mile front there.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:08.688
The good news is that

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.056
the Russians are spread thin.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.057
And what they've got to do,

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.425
they've got to find one place,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.027
a weakness in that front.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.162
And they need to penetrate And in order

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.564
and then they be it,

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.232
they've got to be conducting it

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.967
in an envelopment

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.402
that gets around them

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:23.403
because they're not going to be able

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.804
to go toe to toe with the Russians.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.372
I mean, the Russians are too strong.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.007
They're probably got a couple hundred

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.142
thousand troops in there now.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:29.909
And they're dug in.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.177
They've been there for a year.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.345
They're preparing

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.614
great defensive operations

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.749
and defensive mechanisms in each area.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.884
So they've got to be able

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.652
to find a weakness in the wall.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.753
They've got to penetrate it.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.222
And then you've got to use their superior

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:44.557
maneuver, their ability to integrate

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.525
aviation

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:48.294
ground, direct fire and an indirect fire.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.195
All of that

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.397
and a synergistic effect to defeat

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.234
and envelop the Russian army

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.235
General Steve Anderson,

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.236
always great to talk to you.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.770
Thanks so much for being with us today.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.171
The fog.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:58.871
The mercenary

00:03:58.871 --> 00:03:59.906
chief is slamming

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.140
Russian defense officials

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.843
in a scathing expletive laden tirade

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.345
And he's warning Moscow

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.813
that he will pull his troops

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.881
out of the embattled city of back

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.383
in a matter of days

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.385
due to lack of ammunition.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.152
And new video

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.921
posted to social media Yevgeny

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.156
Prigozhin points to what he says

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.625
are the dead bodies of Falcons

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.660
fighters and shouts obscenities

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.262
at Russia's military leaders.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.831
We do major

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:25.431
items to

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.299
where

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.300
you think you are

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.669
the masters of this life.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.171
You think you can dispose of their lives

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.041
if you think because you have warehouses

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.643
full of ammunition

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.244
that you have that right.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.446
At San Diego,

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.482
the Kremlin is declining to comment.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.350
But Kiev is calling the new decision

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.452
to withdraw from a possible

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.620
turning point.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.588
CNN's Nic Robertson

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.723
joins me now live in eastern Ukraine.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.691
Nic, given

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:52.759
how many months

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.361
we've been speaking about back foot for,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.195
this seems like

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.598
a very significant announcement.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.600
What's your assessment?

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.804
It seems to point at a significant rift

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.006
within the military hierarchy,

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.941
albeit to that.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.343
Yevgeny Prigozhin Wagner

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.612
boss is not in the military structure

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:13.579
at all.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.481
He has actually just in the past

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:19.385
a day also recruited the deputy

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.820
defense minister who was

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.655
who was let go from his position

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.956
only last week.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.658
So it does seem to indicate

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.959
that he has some favor

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.195
within the military hierarchy,

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.230
but specifically in that video

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.432
calling out the defense

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.966
minister, Sergei Shoigu,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:37.704
the Army defense chief of chief of staff,

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.840
Vasily Garrus himself, calling him out,

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.910
laying at their feet specifically

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.545
that they're allowing his fighters

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.045
to die.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.847
Now, Ukrainian officials,

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.582
as you say, is saying perhaps

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.017
if the Russians don't

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.585
turn around their ammunition

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:53.419
supply and back

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.054
would which they assess

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.589
that Wagner has been

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.825
in the vanguard of that fight

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:01.561
for a good part of the last nine months,

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.029
a significant reason,

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:03.563
they say,

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:05.698
why the Russians have been able

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.233
to take so much ground, in fact.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.267
But they say if they

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.503
if the Russians don't turn around

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.271
that that ammunition supply,

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:12.905
then indeed

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.507
this could be a turning point

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.142
for Ukrainian forces.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:20.213
The assessment is that potentially Wagner

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.614
here is

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:22.982
Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.151
and the company itself is recognizing

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.754
that they are being so badly

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.822
decimated, losing so many people.

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.157
One Ukrainian official said

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:33.292
if he is losing 100 a day men.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.927
That's the level they see it.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.496
If he is losing that many a day,

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:37.997
he cannot sustain it.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.799
And this will break the Wagner

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:40.633
organization.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.335
So he has no option to leave.

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.070
But I think there's a telling line

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:44.704
in what is going to be,

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.639
Prigozhin said later today

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.307
following that threat to pull out,

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.909
he said We will go away

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.712
to lick our wounds and we'll rise again

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:54.981
when the Russian nation needs us,

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.716
when the Russian nation.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.118
So he is appealing to others

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.053
outside of the Kremlin.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.388
So this ends

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:05.224
strongly of a significant rift

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.193
that is really thrusting itself into

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:08.561
and into public.

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:09.962
Just when it appeared

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.264
that Russia was getting closer

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:11.898
to actually

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:13.633
being able to take the whole look back,

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:14.834
that's now in question.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:15.334
And that's

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.636
very significant for the

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:18.271
for the Ukrainian counteroffensive

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.238
if it's coming as well.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.541
Yeah, fascinating,

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.242
Nick, seeing the domestic

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:24.544
political turmoil

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:26.412
playing out on the battlefield as well.

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.613
CNN's Nic Robertson for us

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.583
in Eastern Ukraine. Thank you.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.852
On the heels of the alleged drone strike

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.220
in the Kremlin, a warning

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.488
today from the Russian deputy

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:36.255
foreign minister

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:37.590
about worsening relations

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.826
between Moscow and Washington.

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:40.293
Sergei

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.128
Ryabkov says that the two countries

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.564
are on the verge of open armed conflict.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.232
He tells state run media

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:47.467
that Washington has long

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.868
been a direct party

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.336
to the Ukrainian conflict,

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:52.672
and he says that it seeks to destroy

00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:54.173
a sovereign Russia.

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.274
Alex Marquardt joins me now

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.510
from Washington with more on this.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.077
Alex, obviously

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.146
this is a deeply terrifying statement

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:00.580
to hear.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:01.314
We know that Russia's

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.516
rhetoric can often be bellicose.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.917
But help us understand

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:05.751
why it would even be in

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:06.919
Russia's interest

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:09.655
to make these unsubstantiated claims

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.224
and essentially suggest

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:12.892
they're on the warpath with the world's

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.094
most powerful military.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:17.630
Well, the simple answer is to justify

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.199
some kind of escalate escalation

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:23.102
and increased attacks on on Ukraine

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.171
and Kiev itself.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.240
This really is escalatory language.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:27.640
Bianca

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.742
it is extraordinary to hear Russia

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:32.411
not just accuse the U.S.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:33.346
of really

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:35.147
being the power behind Ukraine,

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.048
but accuse the U.S.

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:37.517
of having direct involvement

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:38.851
for having a hand in

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:40.052
what the Kremlin has called

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:42.455
an act of terrorism,

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:44.690
an attempted assassination

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.225
of the Russian president.

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.460
At the same time,

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.095
It is very much in line with what

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:49.962
we have heard

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:51.664
for the past 15 months of this war,

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.666
that it is really the US and Naito

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.201
that are telling Ukraine what to do.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:55.868
And Russia

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:56.469
is in fact

00:08:56.469 --> 00:08:58.538
fighting against all of naito

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:01.507
in there in their war in Ukraine.

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:02.341
Now, of course,

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.509
this has been forcefully

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.511
rejected by the United States.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:05.912
The U.S.

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:07.513
says they are still very much

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:08.414
looking into

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:10.983
what happened at the Kremlin

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.285
two nights ago.

00:09:12.285 --> 00:09:14.520
They are poring over intelligence,

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.022
but the White House has said

00:09:16.022 --> 00:09:16.889
quite forcefully

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:18.157
that the US, of course,

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.625
had no hand in this

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:20.793
and have said what

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:22.795
Russia is accusing them of

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.163
are ludicrous lies.

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:25.565
Take a listen to a bit more of

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:26.766
the White House's John Kirby

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:29.035
Look, I know

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:30.002
there's been
a lot of questions

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:32.538
over the last 24 hours or so

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:33.873
about this alleged

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:35.908
drone attack at the Kremlin.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:36.976
We're still

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:38.077
trying to gather information

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:38.911
about what happened,

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:39.879
and we just don't have

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.681
conclusive evidence one way or the other.

00:09:41.681 --> 00:09:42.882
I know there's lots of questions,

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:43.783
but we just don't have

00:09:43.783 --> 00:09:44.850
conclusive evidence.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.253
One thing I can tell you for certain

00:09:47.253 --> 00:09:48.187
is that the United States

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:49.622
was not involved in this incident

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:52.325
in any way, contrary to Mr. Peskov lies.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:55.494
And that's what they are, just lies.

00:09:55.728 --> 00:09:56.963
So Peskov,

00:09:56.963 --> 00:09:58.965
the Kremlin spokesman,

00:09:58.965 --> 00:09:59.765
was the first person

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:01.067
to make these accusations.

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:02.602
He did not present any evidence

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:03.569
of any U.S.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:04.103
involvement.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.771
And, of course, Bianca, we've heard

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.807
Ukraine deny any involvement,

00:10:07.807 --> 00:10:08.941
not just publicly

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.009
President Zelensky himself

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:11.611
denying it publicly, but privately.

00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:12.912
We are told

00:10:12.912 --> 00:10:13.679
that the

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:14.614
that in conversations

00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:15.514
between Washington

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:16.949
and Kiev, that Ukrainian officials

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:18.551
have told the White House

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:20.920
that they had no role in this either.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:22.955
I was also told by a U.S.

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:23.322
official

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:24.390
that in those conversations

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.858
with Ukrainian officials

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.893
that those Ukrainian officials appeared

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:28.794
rather surprised

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:30.796
and caught off guard by this. Bianca,

00:10:32.098 --> 00:10:33.065
Alex Marquardt for us

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:34.500
in Washington, thank you so much.

